q=A.a([A.N("The home screen lists classroom lessons. Tap a row to play.\n\nA dim card is resting. The Zzz and the number are the days until it recommends you come back. Stars under the title show how far that lesson has come. They do not change the puzzle. The puzzle piece is composition. Headphones mean this visit is listening. The sentence mark means this visit is word order. A photo mark means the lesson is pictures: either one picture and one word, or a scene where the app moves between the things in the picture. Talk-about cards also show a speech bubble.\n\nA lock means the lesson is still ahead in the suggested order. You can open a sleeping lesson or a locked one and drill anyway. A sleeping lesson can also review the last run. That only browses the answers, and the sleep stays as it is.\n\nLeave Due first on, and keep sleeping lessons hidden, so the first card is the next lesson to review. Show sleeping lessons and switch back to catalog order when you want an overview of the whole course.",p,p,p,p,m,p,p,p,p),B.bk],r)
